WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:05.780
basically the idea is to push people toward imagining what they've never imagined

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:11.000
and feeling what they've never felt before

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:47.740
he's an old friend of all of ours, so I'd like you all to welcome.. Timothy Leary

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:55.000
yeah

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:57.020
yeah

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:08.640
I for one, am overjoyed to be here

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:16.720
this is one of those special, special evenings

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:18.400
that we will all treasure

00:03:20.794 --> 00:03:24.094
Terence McKenna means a great deal to me

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:29.000
I would say he's one of the 5 or 6 most important people on the planet

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:36.080
I can't even think of any others..

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:40.460
short term memory loss, but..

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:50.220
Terence and I keep meeting in the most wonderful, mythic, adventurous places

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:52.840
I was doing a wild tour

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:55.840
through Germany about a year ago

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:59.880
we came to Heidelberg and we were being guested by

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.900
some people that came right out of Hermann Hesse..

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:08.180
I mean wizards and gnomes and you know that sort of thing, Heidelberg!

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:10.740
and there was Terence McKenna

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:15.100
and it was just so perfectly Hesse, Journey To The East, yeah..

00:04:16.713 --> 00:04:19.533
and so we meet again here tonight

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:21.620
you know..

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:26.460
I was talking to Terence backstage before we began

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:31.780
and we both agree that what he'll be saying tonight has been said

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:34.460
over and over again

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:36.700
at all those high moments in human history

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:38.780
when those who have gone within

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.080
and understood about the brain

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:44.680
and the inner treasures

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:47.540
we all come back and pretty much say the same thing

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:50.820
but the problem is though that once you say it, you know

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:53.340
you can't go on saying it and saying it and saying it

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:56.960
and when Terence came along a few years ago

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:59.560
and was saying what I've been trying to say

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:03.920
but naturally better, upgraded, up to date

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:06.600
I was so overwhelmed with gratitude

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:09.560
and I publicly thank you for that, Terence

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:16.580
by the way the role that Terence is playing right now

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:20.700
is one that takes not only vision, but it also takes fucking courage

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:29.680
we were saying backstage that

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:32.300
that Terence and I are a

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:34.460
small group of philosophers

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:37.740
who make our living not in the Ivory Tower

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:40.214
-to call it living, but uh..-

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:43.180
just speaking it

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:45.640
chatting it, raving it..

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:48.120
ranting it

00:05:48.568 --> 00:05:51.568
and no one has ever done it with more

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:55.260
poetry and elegance than the speaker tonight

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:58.320
I'm gonna say one more thing and then

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:01.920
we will have what we've all been waiting for

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:04.120
Terence reminds us that

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:07.920
all human wisdom, all energy comes from

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:11.440
our beloved synergetic partners

00:06:11.634 --> 00:06:13.654
the vegetable queendom

00:06:14.118 --> 00:06:16.198
it all comes from the plants

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:18.540
now a round of applause

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:20.280
to the vegetables!

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:27.060
now we all know

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:30.540
that the human body, we have to have food

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:32.060
it comes from vegetables

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:34.680
we've used vegetables over the years

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:36.740
the essence of vegetables in the form of wood

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:39.000
to develop fire, gas, oil, so forth

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:41.560
but what we forget

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:45.040
and what we look to Terence for tonight

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:46.900
is to be reminded that

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:49.648
plants have given us an even more important gift

00:06:49.648 --> 00:06:51.628
they give us the gift of vision

00:06:51.628 --> 00:06:53.468
they give us the illumination

00:06:53.468 --> 00:06:54.363
and throughout human history

00:06:54.363 --> 00:06:56.323
they're at the ease and the pandoras

00:06:56.323 --> 00:06:58.343
usually it's a woman

00:06:58.343 --> 00:07:00.314
who takes this wonderful vegetable

00:07:00.314 --> 00:07:02.594
and gives it to humanity and says

00:07:02.653 --> 00:07:04.153
be illuminated

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:07.720
and now for our illumination and our pleasure

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:11.400
please join me in welcoming Terence McKenna

00:07:24.054 --> 00:07:25.574
well I wanna thank Tim

00:07:25.574 --> 00:07:28.074
that was a wonderful introduction

00:07:28.074 --> 00:07:31.434
I'm sure I wouldn't, I know I wouldn't be here tonight

00:07:31.434 --> 00:07:33.554
if it weren't for Tim Leary

00:07:33.554 --> 00:07:35.414
he was the pathfinder

00:07:35.414 --> 00:07:38.074
he cut the way through the woods

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:40.480
he gave us all permission to be

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:43.640
very much the people that we are tonight

00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:49.200
and it's wonderful that one Irishman can hand it on to another

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:53.900
and that we can keep it in the bardic tradition

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:05.760
wonderful

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:08.760
I can hardly believe I'm here

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:14.140
I made it past the Camaro Raffle

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:23.100
I survived the offer for reconstructive cosmetic surgery

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:30.040
and I've had my smart drugs for this evening, so..

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:32.000
glad to be here!

00:08:35.540 --> 00:08:38.080
well until a few minutes ago I thought that this was a

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:41.300
45 minute gig, so..

00:08:42.340 --> 00:08:46.160
you get to see grace under pressure this evening

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:49.700
naturally I'm kidding, it doesn't matter how long it goes

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:53.100
we could never get to the bottom of this stuff

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:58.100
nor would we wish to, I think

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:09.120
by coincidence merely, I became 45 yesterday

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:11.220
so..

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:18.500
sort of a good moment to do some summing up

00:09:18.874 --> 00:09:20.874
so in thinking about this talk

00:09:20.874 --> 00:09:24.554
and knowing as I did who would be here

00:09:24.740 --> 00:09:27.460
I thought that I would sort of

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:32.500
orient the theme toward distilling the psychedelic mind

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:34.740
which is a way of

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:37.074
talking about the psychedelic mind

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:38.360
but also

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:40.540
trying to, uh..

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:45.020
considering the amount of money you paid for this session

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:49.880
give you the entire shtick in one fell swoop

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:52.540
so that you would never have to

00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:55.720
attend a Terence McKenna lecture

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:57.860
or workshop again

00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:01.220
you can just move past that

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:05.560
turn the page on that kind of thing in your life

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:12.800
with me in the studio is Terence McKenna

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:16.300
author, lecturer, explorer and philosopher

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:19.674
Terence is the co-author with his brother Dennis McKenna

00:10:19.674 --> 00:10:24.254
of a book called 'The Invisible Landscape: Mind, Hallucinogens, and the I Ching'

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:28.800
he is also the co-author of 'Psilocybin: Magic Mushroom Grower's Guide'

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:32.580
he is the author of a computer program called Timewave Zero

00:10:32.626 --> 00:10:34.226
and he is the co-founder

00:10:34.340 --> 00:10:36.620
and president of an organisation called

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:38.340
Botanical Dimensions

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:40.239
which devotes itself to saving

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:42.400
botanical plants

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:45.500
used in shamanistic traditions throughout the world

00:10:45.820 --> 00:10:46.940
welcome Terence

00:10:46.940 --> 00:10:48.260
it's a pleasure to be here

00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:49.740
it's a pleasure to have you here

00:10:57.820 --> 00:11:01.340
well I think the most profound cultural development

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:06.640
it is possible to make the case that language itself

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:11.680
is an ability, that was coaxed out of an

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:14.620
evolving primate species

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:16.660
by virtue of the fact

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:19.400
that there were hallucinogenic plants

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:22.160
in the diet of that creature

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:26.040
you see, psilocybin has been shown in low doses

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:29.240
to actually increase visual acuity

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:33.140
well at the stage of evolution where

00:11:33.140 --> 00:11:36.640
human beings encountered psilocybin mushrooms

00:11:36.780 --> 00:11:45.940
we were essentially, baboon-like, pack-hunting, hoards of velt-living creatures in Africa

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:51.060
in that situation, a compound which increases visual acuity

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:54.140
will give a tremendous adaptive advantage

00:11:54.180 --> 00:11:57.660
to the animals that are including it in their diet

00:11:57.660 --> 00:12:00.900
and those animals not including it in their diet

00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:05.700
will be quickly eliminated by the process of natural selection

00:12:05.960 --> 00:12:08.560
from the evolutionary scenario

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:10.600
so it's possible to argue

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:14.400
that this mind manifesting quality

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:16.340
of the psychedelics

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:21.320
actually conferred an evolutionary advantage

00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:23.333
on certain primates

00:12:23.333 --> 00:12:26.673
who then were able to bootstrap themselves

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:31.440
to higher and higher states of reflective self awareness

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:37.180
this may lie behind the very early coincidence of

00:12:37.180 --> 00:12:41.500
cattle, goddesses and mushrooms

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:45.180
in the apparent obsessions of early man

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:49.920
as reflected by the cave paintings on the Algerian plateau

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:52.720
and in southern France and Spain

00:12:52.740 --> 00:12:56.780
we always find the notion of the mystery

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:59.660
circa 18 thousand years ago

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:02.040
connected with the idea of cattle

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:07.700
and we always find the cattle connected with the notion of the Great Goddess

00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:12.520
now it may be that the hidden and third member of this trinity

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:15.920
was a hallucinogenic mushroom of some sort

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:17.700
we've got only about 2 minutes left

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:20.280
but I wonder what the connection, I don't quite see it

00:13:20.280 --> 00:13:22.840
between the mushroom, the cattle and the Goddess

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:27.460
the mushrooms grow in the manure of the cattle

00:13:27.460 --> 00:13:32.060
when the hunting packs of early primates

00:13:32.260 --> 00:13:34.980
followed along behind the cattle,

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:38.180
they inevitably encountered the mushroom

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:43.560
ate it, had their visual skills thereby increased,

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:50.680
bred more readily therefore and survived more easily than their non-mushroom eating cousins

00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:57.160
and so the eating of mushrooms and the development of higher aspects of consciousness

00:13:57.160 --> 00:14:01.640
including self-reflection, were thereby enforced

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:04.880
leading to the conclusion that it was actually

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:08.840
a symbiotic relationship between early primates

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:11.360
and these hallucinogenic plants

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:16.820
that laid the basis for the appearance of what we call human beings

00:14:16.820 --> 00:14:18.280
well Terence McKenna, this is

00:14:18.280 --> 00:14:19.840
a very interesting discussion

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:23.120
you seem to be suggesting that our evolution, I suppose

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:26.060
from the animal kingdom into the human kingdom itself

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:31.280
was catalysed or triggered by our encounter with these hallucinogenics

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:35.760
yes, we are an ape with a symbiotic relationship

00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:36.960
to a mushroom

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:38.520
and that has given us

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:41.600
self-reflection, language, religion

00:14:41.600 --> 00:14:45.500
and all the spectrum of effects that flow from these things

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:48.480
and one can only wonder how

00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:51.900
these hallucinogens might affect our future evolution as well

00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:56.520
they've brought us to this point, and as we make our relationship to them conscious

00:14:56.540 --> 00:15:01.400
we may be able to take control of our future evolutionary path

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:19.460
in the 120 years from 1500 to the beginning of the 30 years war

00:15:19.500 --> 00:15:24.400
Europe was caught in a number of conspiracies and political intrigues

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:30.920
directed toward moving Europe toward a magical and alchemicly based society

00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:34.720
the protestant princes of the northern league of Germany

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:40.300
especially Frederick the Elector Palatine came to culminate this movement

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:46.980
but its roots lie further back in the 1580s of the 16th century

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:54.400
it was in this period that the english astrologer, astronomer, mathematician, navigator

00:15:54.400 --> 00:15:57.940
and expert of espionage, John Dee

00:15:57.940 --> 00:16:02.320
launched his famous and mysterious mission to Bohemia

00:16:02.320 --> 00:16:05.580
a little-known incident in european history

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:11.620
which holds clues to understanding the faith and evolution of modern science

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:15.960
and the nature of a lost world of magical and alchemical thinking

00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:21.080
that once claimed the attention of the european imagination

00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:26.440
John Dee

00:16:27.020 --> 00:16:29.740
the greatest mind of the Elizabethan era

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:32.280
friend of Queen Elizabeth

00:16:33.140 --> 00:16:35.200
colleague of Sir Philip Sidney

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:39.000
converser with angels

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:41.640
mathematician par excellence

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:47.180
determined under the influence of the mysterious Edward Kelley

00:16:47.300 --> 00:16:51.940
that he was to be the center of an alchemical renaissance

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:55.980
and a secret society that would lay the groundwork

00:16:55.980 --> 00:16:59.640
for the continuation of the dream of Austria

00:17:00.260 --> 00:17:06.060
the dream built around the Elizabethan Queen, Elizabeth I

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:19.700
he associated himself intensely with the Arthurian mythical and mystical side

00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:23.520
of the Elizabethan idea of British Empire

00:17:26.920 --> 00:17:32.340
he was a Welshman, like the Queen, he was so intensely devoted too

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:37.840
and like her, he shared the renaissance mood of saturnian melancholy

00:17:37.900 --> 00:17:39.260
a collector of books,

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:42.080
a builder of scientific instruments,

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:44.940
a composer of codes and cyphers

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:47.460
fascinated with alchemy

00:17:47.760 --> 00:17:52.420
Dee was both the figure of the introspective melancholic

00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:58.320
and the world-planning, empire-building political visionary

00:18:00.660 --> 00:18:04.560
Dee was under the patrionage of the Earl of Northtumberland

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:10.980
and it was Northtumberland who looted the catholic monestaries at the time of Henry VIII

00:18:12.600 --> 00:18:18.260
we have reason to believe that John Dee had virtual Carte Blanche in selecting

00:18:18.260 --> 00:18:21.940
manuscripts from those libraries that interested him

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:31.200
not only was Dee a scholar of the classics

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:33.360
and the magical past

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:39.760
but he was an intimate friend with some of the great movers and shakers of his own time

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:46.780
particularly Sir Philip Sidney and the entire catorioue of poets and artists

00:18:46.780 --> 00:18:53.980
who had gathered themselves around Elizabeth, Austria to celebrate her reign

00:18:53.980 --> 00:19:00.920
and to make of her, the paradigmatic sovereign of Europe that Dee believed led the way

00:19:00.920 --> 00:19:05.520
toward the establishing of a universal alchemical monarchy

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:08.960
it was essentially a poetic enterprise

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:11.340
as alchemy always is

00:19:12.340 --> 00:19:13.720
Merlin

00:19:13.940 --> 00:19:18.200
in the Arthurian legends has come down to us

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:21.500
basically disguised as John Dee

00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:25.900
the image we have of Merlin is Dee's image

00:19:26.420 --> 00:19:33.760
So, Dee possessed an enormous power over the imagination of his contemporaries

00:19:33.760 --> 00:19:36.320
they were in awe of his learning

00:19:46.340 --> 00:19:49.860
perhaps we are the naive ones

00:19:49.860 --> 00:19:56.880
perhaps we too quickly assumed that we had understood all there was to know about matter

00:19:56.880 --> 00:20:00.200
after all, even to this moment

00:20:00.200 --> 00:20:03.980
we cannot locate the seat of the imagination

00:20:03.980 --> 00:20:05.320
in matter

00:20:05.320 --> 00:20:09.800
we cannot trace the evolution of a human thought or hope

00:20:09.800 --> 00:20:11.440
in matter

00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:19.200
it's almost as though the alchemists

00:20:19.200 --> 00:20:22.640
through their humility, had a deeper insight

00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:24.720
into the workings of the world

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:27.540
than we have achieved today

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:45.620
this is ground zero for the Rosicrucian Enlightenment

00:20:54.620 --> 00:20:56.640
standing here,

00:20:56.640 --> 00:20:59.060
in the alchemical laboratory

00:20:59.460 --> 00:21:01.900
of the palace in Heidelberg

00:21:02.140 --> 00:21:09.060
we are essentially at the center of the alchemical hopes of the Rosicrucian Enlightenment

00:21:09.060 --> 00:21:13.360
it was here in the years before the adventure in Bohemia,

00:21:13.360 --> 00:21:18.700
that Frederick's alchemists, astrologers and suit-sayers

00:21:18.700 --> 00:21:24.160
toiled directly under the King's observation and control

00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:26.640
here came Michael Maier

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:28.300
Heinrich Khunrath

00:21:28.660 --> 00:21:31.100
the great names of alchemy

00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:35.420
it's entirely possible that John Dee was in this room

00:21:35.420 --> 00:21:38.380
it's entirely possible that Edward Kelley

00:21:38.680 --> 00:21:41.440
stood were I am standing now

00:21:42.760 --> 00:21:47.660
it's almost impossible to conceive of the hopes and the fantasies

00:21:47.660 --> 00:21:49.520
and the labours

00:21:49.620 --> 00:21:51.240
and the dreams

00:21:51.320 --> 00:21:55.540
that have been generated by and are centered on

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:59.360
this room and the objects in it

00:21:59.360 --> 00:22:04.140
this is the last alchemical laboratory in the world

00:22:04.140 --> 00:22:10.840
to fully function before the rise of modern science

00:22:14.040 --> 00:22:17.260
and these tools in many ways reflect

00:22:17.260 --> 00:22:21.820
the internal cosmology of the man and woman who used them

00:22:21.820 --> 00:22:26.260
this, for example, a typical alchemical distillery

00:22:26.260 --> 00:22:28.720
is called the pelican

00:22:29.120 --> 00:22:34.160
another example of the colourful nature of alchemical vocabulary

00:22:34.160 --> 00:22:43.700
it's called the pelican because it is associated with the myth of a bird which plucks blood from its own breast

00:22:43.700 --> 00:22:45.780
the prima materia

00:22:45.780 --> 00:22:50.500
feces, black coal, charcoal, salt nitrate

00:22:50.500 --> 00:22:51.980
heated in here

00:22:52.280 --> 00:22:57.040
brought to a high temperature, a fevered colouric state

00:22:57.160 --> 00:23:01.240
rises into the higher emporium of the vessel

00:23:01.360 --> 00:23:05.640
and there, rarified, it condenses

00:23:05.820 --> 00:23:07.100
liquifies

00:23:07.180 --> 00:23:13.100
and flows down into the cooler domain of the child of the pelican

00:23:13.260 --> 00:23:17.460
here the essence is collected, the quint-essence

00:23:17.480 --> 00:23:20.780
and always the hope was that

00:23:20.940 --> 00:23:25.480
the next experiment, the next combination of materials

00:23:25.480 --> 00:23:28.420
would yield the elixir vitae

00:23:28.420 --> 00:23:30.640
the lapis philosophorum

00:23:30.640 --> 00:23:33.900
the completion that the alchemists sought

00:23:35.500 --> 00:23:38.420
and so all this fantastic apparatus

00:23:38.420 --> 00:23:40.160
that we see around us

00:23:40.160 --> 00:23:41.360
is really

00:23:41.880 --> 00:23:47.140
not so much in the service of channeling liquids, gasses

00:23:47.460 --> 00:23:50.720
but in the service of channeling spirit

00:23:50.800 --> 00:23:52.360
out of matter

00:23:52.360 --> 00:23:54.420
and into the higher realms

00:23:54.420 --> 00:23:57.520
where it then can be refluxed,

00:23:57.520 --> 00:23:58.852
recondensed

00:23:59.040 --> 00:24:01.840
and the lapis philosophorum

00:24:01.840 --> 00:24:03.960
the stone of the philosophers

00:24:04.040 --> 00:24:05.400
the central mystery

00:24:05.780 --> 00:24:07.740
brought to completion

00:24:19.820 --> 00:24:22.680
the transformation of matter

00:24:22.680 --> 00:24:27.880
into a universal panacea for the redemption of mankind

00:24:28.120 --> 00:24:32.720
this was Dee's great passion

00:24:32.720 --> 00:24:36.480
this was the overarching theme of his life

00:24:36.480 --> 00:24:39.440
a deep, deep commitment

00:24:39.440 --> 00:24:41.680
to the reformation of society

00:24:41.680 --> 00:24:46.780
and a deep, deep exhaustion and rejection

00:24:46.780 --> 00:24:52.420
of the values of Christendom that he saw betrayed all about him

00:24:56.600 --> 00:24:58.280
and then by distillation

00:24:58.500 --> 00:25:00.960
and then by coagulation

00:25:01.020 --> 00:25:04.080
and then by concentration through firing

00:25:04.240 --> 00:25:07.960
the alchemical body is brought to completion

00:25:07.980 --> 00:25:10.780
these are processes that go on both within

00:25:10.780 --> 00:25:13.500
the chemical retort, the alembic,

00:25:13.500 --> 00:25:15.580
in the alchemist's laboratory

00:25:15.580 --> 00:25:19.880
and they're processes which go on in the heart and mind

00:25:20.000 --> 00:25:21.740
of the alchemist

00:25:23.740 --> 00:25:26.420
one process dissolves

00:25:26.440 --> 00:25:30.480
another process separates the dross,

00:25:30.480 --> 00:25:33.180
the gross matter from the precious

00:25:33.180 --> 00:25:36.900
another concentrates the subtle essence

00:25:36.900 --> 00:25:42.620
another raises the subtle essence to another level of refinement

00:25:51.300 --> 00:25:54.140
and over time

00:25:54.160 --> 00:25:56.400
the great friend of the alchemist

00:25:56.560 --> 00:25:59.400
this process of rarifaction

00:25:59.408 --> 00:26:00.560
and growth

00:26:00.560 --> 00:26:02.900
both metallic and psychological

00:26:02.960 --> 00:26:05.920
both internal and external

00:26:06.660 --> 00:26:10.740
both personal and impersonal

00:26:11.060 --> 00:26:14.780
proceeds and feeds upon itself

00:26:14.820 --> 00:26:21.260
and eventually, not through an illogic discernable to the scientific mind

00:26:21.260 --> 00:26:25.240
there is a kind of miracle

00:26:25.240 --> 00:26:27.500
the production of the stone

00:26:27.500 --> 00:26:30.220
the union of spirit and matter

00:26:30.220 --> 00:26:38.360
the fusion of these two contradictory aspects of the universe into a new and third thing

00:26:38.360 --> 00:26:39.960
the quintessence

00:26:39.960 --> 00:26:41.420
the rubedo

00:26:41.520 --> 00:26:43.500
the lapis philosophorum

00:26:43.500 --> 00:26:44.980
the aqua vitae

00:26:44.980 --> 00:26:48.440
the nostre lapis philosophorum devici

00:26:54.580 --> 00:27:00.420
one of the most famous of all alchemical axioms is

00:27:00.420 --> 00:27:04.100
as above, so below

00:27:04.100 --> 00:27:05.980
meaning always

00:27:05.980 --> 00:27:09.440
that in every small part of reality

00:27:09.600 --> 00:27:12.300
there is a tiny reflection

00:27:12.600 --> 00:27:16.980
of the great over structure of reality

00:27:16.980 --> 00:27:21.840
and in the larger structures are hidden the secrets of the smallest

00:27:21.840 --> 00:27:23.720
and vice versa

00:27:30.260 --> 00:27:33.780
we have unconsciously imbibed the ontology of science

00:27:33.900 --> 00:27:38.100
where we have mind firmly separated out from the world

00:27:38.813 --> 00:27:40.413
but in an earlier age

00:27:40.540 --> 00:27:45.800
mind and matter were seem to be out loyed together throughout nature

00:27:52.060 --> 00:28:00.000
and I think it's very interesting that at this very high-tech moment in our adventure

00:28:01.100 --> 00:28:03.940
the plants return

00:28:03.940 --> 00:28:09.160
and almost stand before us as a beacon

00:28:09.160 --> 00:28:10.640
and a promise

00:28:10.800 --> 00:28:14.080
they stand for absolute Tao

00:28:14.400 --> 00:28:15.860
they stand

00:28:15.962 --> 00:28:18.800
for the correct way

00:28:18.800 --> 00:28:24.018
for life to relate to its environment

00:28:39.680 --> 00:28:44.300
this is one of the most interesting new psychedelics in the world

00:28:44.360 --> 00:28:46.920
this is salvia divinorum

00:28:46.920 --> 00:28:54.960
and it is definitely one of the plants which will shape the next few decades of the new millenium

00:28:57.760 --> 00:28:59.880
this is a coleus

00:29:00.100 --> 00:29:02.660
it's ironic that these plants

00:29:02.660 --> 00:29:09.440
which have been in our kitchens and in our windowsill flowerbeds for generations

00:29:09.440 --> 00:29:15.620
turn out to contain psycho-active compounds as powerful as any known to science

00:29:16.660 --> 00:29:20.000
these are not particularly interesting in terms of drugs

00:29:20.000 --> 00:29:22.260
but they're certainly bizarre

00:29:24.980 --> 00:29:27.820
climb up here, with me

00:29:28.480 --> 00:29:31.740
this is one of the most interesting plants in the garden

00:29:31.740 --> 00:29:34.080
this is Psychotria viridis

00:29:34.080 --> 00:29:37.220
this is the plant which causes the vision

00:29:37.420 --> 00:29:39.440
when taken with Ayahuasca

00:29:39.440 --> 00:29:41.180
when taken as a liquid

00:29:41.180 --> 00:29:44.320
the experience lasts about 4-6 hours

00:29:44.440 --> 00:29:46.898
it's not as intense as smoking it

00:29:46.898 --> 00:29:50.018
smoking it is the most intense experience

00:29:50.140 --> 00:29:53.040
this side of the yawning grave

00:29:53.380 --> 00:29:57.520
when I take psychedelics I always do it in a shamanic style

00:29:57.840 --> 00:29:59.540
usually at night

00:29:59.680 --> 00:30:01.280
usually alone

00:30:01.455 --> 00:30:04.275
in nature, if possible

00:30:04.400 --> 00:30:07.020
and then I watch

00:30:08.720 --> 00:30:10.800
I pay very close attention

00:30:11.200 --> 00:30:15.080
I use my mind as an alchemical vessel

00:30:15.080 --> 00:30:17.780
for carrying out observations

00:30:17.780 --> 00:30:20.380
on the union of spirit

00:30:20.380 --> 00:30:22.720
my spirit, my personality

00:30:22.720 --> 00:30:24.240
and matter

00:30:24.240 --> 00:30:26.100
the physical matter

00:30:26.100 --> 00:30:29.520
of the substance that I'm ingesting

00:30:41.440 --> 00:30:46.280
building on western psychotherapy as elaborated by Freud and Jung

00:30:46.600 --> 00:30:49.120
one view of what psychedelics are

00:30:49.120 --> 00:30:54.120
is, it's the part of your mind that you'd rather not do business with

00:30:54.120 --> 00:30:59.320
it's the memories of childhood neglect or abuse,

00:30:59.320 --> 00:31:04.920
it's uh, repressed kinky fantasies

00:31:04.920 --> 00:31:09.440
in other words, the Freudian idea of the unconscious

00:31:09.457 --> 00:31:15.132
that somehow these are drugs which dissolve the boundary between conscious and unconscious mind

00:31:15.132 --> 00:31:18.692
and then you can do excellerated psychotherapy

00:31:18.692 --> 00:31:22.600
cause resistances have been pharmacologically overcome

00:31:22.600 --> 00:31:24.240
that's one model

00:31:24.240 --> 00:31:28.400
it's good as far as it goes, it just doesn't go far enough

00:31:28.400 --> 00:31:31.320
then there's another model

00:31:31.600 --> 00:31:36.920
which I would call the traditional or shamanic model

00:31:36.920 --> 00:31:39.080
and it says

00:31:39.080 --> 00:31:42.600
the cosmos is a series of levels

00:31:42.600 --> 00:31:51.880
and these levels are connected by vertical routes of access

00:31:51.880 --> 00:31:56.040
which can be thought of as simply flights through space,

00:31:56.040 --> 00:31:58.320
or magical trees,

00:31:58.320 --> 00:32:00.600
or magical ladders,

00:32:00.600 --> 00:32:03.480
anyway, there's an image of ascent

00:32:03.480 --> 00:32:08.960
and ordinary people exist on only one of these levels

00:32:08.960 --> 00:32:14.920
but a shaman is not an ordinary person, a shaman is a superhuman person

00:32:14.920 --> 00:32:20.280
who has the power of animal allies behind them

00:32:20.280 --> 00:32:28.440
and they can go up and down in these elevators that move between levels

00:32:28.440 --> 00:32:33.280
and they can therefore recover lost souls,

00:32:33.280 --> 00:32:39.880
see social hanky panky, theft and adultery,

00:32:39.880 --> 00:32:42.320
see the causes behind that,

00:32:42.325 --> 00:32:44.485
see the causes behind disease

00:32:44.485 --> 00:32:46.285
so forth and so on

00:32:46.285 --> 00:32:48.925
that would be the traditional one

00:32:48.925 --> 00:32:52.925
well, thinking about this from a mathematicians' point of view

00:32:53.320 --> 00:33:01.160
an all-encompassing explanation that would explain how all these magical feats are done

00:33:01.160 --> 00:33:05.960
is simply to suppose that the shaman is somehow able

00:33:05.961 --> 00:33:11.001
to project his consciousness, his or her consciousness,

00:33:11.001 --> 00:33:13.401
into a higher dimension

00:33:13.760 --> 00:33:20.440
not metaphorically, as in 'Sylvester Stallone has many dimensions'

00:33:20.440 --> 00:33:22.280
not metaphorically

00:33:22.280 --> 00:33:28.920
but literally, as in 'One dimension, two dimensions, three dimensions and four..

00:33:29.040 --> 00:33:34.960
then I have noticed that all of biology

00:33:34.960 --> 00:33:39.360
not simply shamanism within the context of human society

00:33:39.360 --> 00:33:43.440
but all of biology is, in a sense,

00:33:43.440 --> 00:33:47.080
a conquest of dimensionality

00:33:47.080 --> 00:33:50.440
that, as we ascend

00:33:50.440 --> 00:33:53.880
the phylogeny of organic life,

00:33:53.880 --> 00:34:00.985
what animals are, are a strategy for conquering space-time

00:34:00.985 --> 00:34:05.665
and complex animals do it better than simpler animals

00:34:05.680 --> 00:34:09.200
and we do it better than any complex animal,

00:34:09.200 --> 00:34:15.400
and we, 20th-century people do it better than any people in any previous century

00:34:15.402 --> 00:34:20.082
because we combined data in so many ways that they couldn't:

00:34:20.082 --> 00:34:24.442
electronically, on film, on tape, so forth and so on

